From 3d57550d3fcb42ccbb1172c3e19ea4a5b177aa7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pcDuino3B Armbian CI <noreply@github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun7i: pcduino3: switch GMAC to RGMII for 3B

The LinkSprite pcDuino3B replaces the original pcDuino3 10/100 PHY
interface with a Gigabit Ethernet PHY wired through RGMII.  The board
layout follows the pcDuino3, while its GMAC wiring matches pcDuino3
Nano for this interface.

Use the A20 RGMII pin group and RGMII internal-delay mode so the
stmmac/PHY stack can negotiate 1000BASE-T on pcDuino3B.

This patch is intentionally carried as an Armbian userpatch because the
upstream sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts continues to describe the original
(non-3B) board.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-pcduino3.dts
@@ -121,10 +121,10 @@ &ehci1 {
 
 &gmac {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&gmac_mii_pins>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&gmac_rgmii_pins>;
 	phy-handle = <&phy1>;
-	phy-mode = "mii";
+	phy-mode = "rgmii-id";
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &i2c0 {
